From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WinterMist010 <85207868+WinterMist010@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] tu/a8xx: reset the LRZ controls after the end-of-pass flush

The end-of-pass LRZ_FLUSH is asynchronous: it writes the fast-clear
state back to memory while the next render pass may already bind a
different LRZ buffer.  If the flushed buffer had a large
fast-cleared area (about 512 bytes of fast-clear flags per layer and
up), the flush can still be in flight when the next pass changes the
LRZ state, and the GPU hangs with VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST.

freedreno already resets the LRZ controls at the start of every
batch (fd6_lrz_inv()) for the same reason.  Do the equivalent at the
end of the pass on A8XX: write zero to GRAS_LRZ_CNTL/GRAS_LRZ_CNTL2
so the flush completes before the next pass touches LRZ.

A WFI or a second LRZ_FLUSH also fixes the hang; the register reset
is the cheapest and matches freedreno.

Ported from the Droid-Deck/Drivers series (patches/lrz/0001,
reported on Adreno 840 where it reproduced in The Message from Deep
Space); the workaround is gated on CHIP >= A8XX.

---
  src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc | 12 ++++++++++++
  1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc
index ec556403420..ee2ef16736b 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_lrz.cc
@@ -934,6 +934,18 @@ tu_lrz_tiling_end(struct tu_cmd_buffer *cmd, struct tu_cs *cs)
    } else {
       tu_emit_event_write<CHIP>(cmd, cs, FD_LRZ_FLUSH);
    }
+
+   /* The LRZ_FLUSH above is asynchronous: it writes the fast-clear state back
+    * to memory while the next render pass may already be binding a different
+    * LRZ buffer.  If the flushed buffer had a large fast-cleared area, the
+    * flush can still be in flight when the next pass changes the LRZ state and
+    * the GPU hangs (device-lost).  freedreno resets the LRZ controls at the
+    * start of every batch (fd6_lrz_inv()) for the same reason, so do the
+    * equivalent here: writing zero to GRAS_LRZ_CNTL/GRAS_LRZ_CNTL2 makes the
+    * flush complete before the next pass touches LRZ.
+    */
+   if (CHIP >= A8XX)
+      tu6_write_lrz_cntl<CHIP>(cmd, cs, {});
 }
 TU_GENX(tu_lrz_tiling_end);
 
